**Proposition 8.1 (actual original-source realization and exact
alphabet accounting).** Let $B\subseteq S_d^n$ be one of the
nonempty solution fibers in Definition 4.1, Definition 5.1, or
Lemma 7.2 and its products. Put $H=\lceil\log_2n\rceil$,
$N=2^H$, $D=H+d$. Pad the remaining $N-n$ positions with the
fixed tree $\alpha$, and place these $N$ blocks at the frontier
of a public perfect right-subtree scaffold of height $H$. There
is a correct preparation/reader on the entire $\mathcal F_D$
with attained alphabet exactly

$$
|S_D|-|B|+1,
\tag{INB.35}
$$

merging precisely these $|B|$ canonical states into one name and
giving every other canonical state its own name. A sufficient
preparation on every source uses exactly

$$
2^D-1\text{ Reads},\qquad
\text{maximum literal length }D,\qquad
(D-1)2^D+1\text{ submitted letters}.
\tag{INB.36}
$$

After any original late request it makes zero Reads or one actual
original-root Read of length at most $D$ on the same stationary
source, before its reply and before any authentic count.

Proof. This is the paid full-family construction of CBN Theorem 7.1,
Proposition 7.2 and GCB §5, applied to the specified fibers. Here are
its exact hypotheses and substitution. At public frontier addresses
$a_i$ of length $H$, insert the actual trees $x_i$ from $B$ and
the fixed padding. These are distinct canonical states of $S_D$:
ordered assembly is injective, each inserted block is in $S_d$,
and the height is at most $H+d$. Call their image $\widehat B$.
Targets strictly above the frontier are branch constants; those
inside padding have fixed full factors, including initially absent
ones. Every remaining target is $Ra_iq$, $q\in W_d$, and inherits
the complete witness for block $i$. A donor $(j,b)$ is the actual
word $Ra_jb$, of length at most $1+H+d-1=D$. All these occurrences
are present; no absent position is transported as a subtree.

Their trajectories agree with the local ones by homomorphic
transport at the present occurrence. This is exactly the presence
premise of `original_present_transport` in [NativeDepthPatterns][D5N].
The complete supplied $\Gamma$ decoder then handles every authentic
subsequent count. For a canonical singleton every factor is already
known from its name and needs no Read. Thus the one merged fiber
and all other singletons are a complete admissible canonical partition.

To obtain its name without advice, before receiving $p$ submit all
original-root $Rq$ with $q\in W_D$, including absent replies, in a
fixed public order. The acquired boundary determines $\pi_D(v)$
by the credited canonical reconstruction, hence its name. The call
count is $\sum_{l=0}^{D-1}2^l=2^D-1$, and the letter count is
$\sum_{l=0}^{D-1}(l+1)2^l=(D-1)2^D+1$; the latter follows
by induction, adding $(D+1)2^D$ at the next depth. The maximum
length is $D$. This is a deterministic effective terminating scan,
independent of both source replies and the later request.

Install the finite public witness and membership tables and compute
a fixed-width name. Export that name alone. The paid isolation
removes the scan, temporary arrays, selectors and other accessible
source dependence; control, allocation and computation can use a
public padded finite schedule. Canonicalization preserves all
boundary replies and all requested factors. Therefore the same
zero-Read or one-Read witness works on every original source in
the inverse image of a name, even when its unrepresented deeper
labels differ. Its literal is selected using only the complete
name, $D,p$ and installed tables, before reply or count. The
source never changes and no prior transcript is accessible.

Every canonical state is attained by taking $v$ equal to it.
There is one name for $\widehat B$, whose size is $|B|$, and
one per other canonical state. Hence the complete attained alphabet
is exactly (INB.35). Its merged fiber on $\mathcal F_D$ is the
full inverse image under $\pi_D$, not just the displayed physical
canonical sources. $\square$

